Task: Migrate GraphQL to REST with minimal code changes.

1. Find all GraphQL queries, mutations, subscriptions, Apollo usage, generated GraphQL types, and GraphQL-specific services.
2. For each GraphQL operation, identify the equivalent REST endpoint I provide.
3. Replace GraphQL calls with the existing Angular REST/HttpClient pattern already used in this project.
4. Reuse a shared REST service where multiple components/states call the same backend area. Do not duplicate endpoint construction or HTTP logic.
5. Preserve existing public method names, NGXS actions, state structure, component behavior, loading behavior, and error handling unless a change is required.
6. Remove GraphQL response wrappers such as response.data.xxx. Map the REST response directly to the existing application model.
7. Do not use any. Reuse existing interfaces/models when possible; create a new REST response interface only when necessary.
8. Do not refactor unrelated code.
9. After all GraphQL calls are migrated, remove unused GraphQL code:
    * Apollo services/imports
    * GraphQL queries/mutations
    * generated GraphQL files/types that are no longer referenced
    * GraphQL configuration/providers
    * GraphQL environment/config values
    * GraphQL npm dependencies
10. Before deleting a dependency/file, search the entire project and confirm it has no remaining references.
11. Update affected unit tests to mock REST/HttpClient instead of Apollo/GraphQL.
12. Keep changes small and production-safe.
13. Do not create documentation unless requested.
14. Do not explain unchanged code.